+// Whether the underlying decoder filter has failed. A failed decoder filter
+// may still end its output with a normal EOF; callers must treat such an EOF
+// as a playback error rather than as a normal end of the stream.
+// This consumes the pending failure notification, so it must only be called
+// when the caller immediately transitions to a terminal error path. Must not
+// be called from the decoder thread.
+bool mp_decoder_wrapper_has_failed(struct mp_decoder_wrapper *d);
